menu "CampusPulse bounded T-Energy acceptance"
config TE_SMALL_CLEAR_LEGACY_SCANSTATS
    bool "Maintenance image: delete only the authorized legacy scanstats/devs key"
    default n
    help
        Explicit operator-authorized maintenance image, not a normal runtime
        feature. Verify the existing 12300-byte BLOB read-only, then erase only
        scanstats/devs through the SDK and commit/read back NOT_FOUND. Never
        erase a namespace, partition, other key, or queue. No BLE/Wi-Fi starts.
        After reporting numeric before/after statistics, remain in USB standby.
        Mutually exclusive with the window-reboot checkpoint image.
config TE_SMALL_TEST_HOLD_FIRST_COMMIT
    bool "Hold after the first committed window for normal-reboot acceptance"
    default n
    help
        Explicit physical acceptance image only. Requires max_windows=1. After
        committing/reopening and releasing that exact window, pause capture
        and hold without POST or more NVS writes until a physical reset. The
        next boot recovers the old exact record before registering new work.
        This is a normal-reboot checkpoint, not arbitrary power-loss acceptance.
endmenu
